            <ArticleTitle>A nursing approach to pain in older adults.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>77-82; quiz 83</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Persistent pain is a barrier to healthy aging. Nurses are in a unique position to assist older adults with pain to remain active and promote their well-being. Barrett's (1998) power-as-knowing participation-in-change theory can help nurses appreciate the contributions older people make, and mutually explore with them their options and choices regarding pain and their lifestyle.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
